      "additionalTabs": {
        "0": {
          "id": "_notes-_1767322477683",
          "name": "Rules"
        },
        "1": {
          "id": "_1786624926271",
          "name": "Values Log",
          "defaultNotes": {
            "0": {
              "label": "Advancement",
              "value": null,
              "locked": true
            },
            "1": {
              "label": "Will",
              "value": null,
              "locked": true
            },
            "2": {
              "label": "Loyalty",
              "value": null,
              "locked": true
            },
            "3": {
              "label": "The World",
              "value": null,
              "locked": true
            },
            "4": {
              "label": "Truth",
              "value": null,
              "locked": true
            },
            "5": {
              "label": "Connection",
              "value": null,
              "locked": true
            }
          },
          "description": "<p>You can challenge a Value Statement (act against your own Value) when you have the spotlight:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Roll three dice for that Value instead of one</li>\n<li>Step the Value down</li>\n</ul>\n<p>At the end of the session either tewrite the Value Statement and recover the dice, or keep the value and:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Step up another Value.</li>\n<li>Record the act you took against the Value you just stepped up in the Value Log.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>If you step up a Value beyond a D12 you must read to the table the Value Log.&nbsp; The other players will then reach a vote how you transcend the value.</p>"
        },
        "2": {
          "id": "_1787056762781",
          "name": "Session Log",
          "description": "<p>Record key events from a session, one session per section.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Callback</strong>: reference a previously recorded session during play as you act as an in-character nod to the past.&nbsp; Gain a benfit equal to anything a Plot Point could bye (byt do not gain a Plot Point).&nbsp; Each past session can only be called back once per session.</li>\n<li><strong>Training Up</strong>: Spend recorded sessions to make improvements to your character.&nbsp; Once a session has been used for training up it can no longer be used as a Callback.</li>\n</ul>\n<table style=\"width: 91.5162%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 66.0356%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.9644%;\"></colgroup>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Improvement</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Cost</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Turn a scene Asset into a Signature Asset</td>\n<td>1 session</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Switch out a Distinction for a new one</td>\n<td>1 session</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Step up a Signature Asset</td>\n<td>2 sessions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Unlock a new SFX</td>\n<td>2 sessions</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Step up a Kill</td>\n<td>3 sessions</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>"
        },
        "3": {
          "id": "_1786624946207",
          "name": "Notes"
        }
      }
    },
